000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  \u000apatient's name and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "Left breast blue", consists of two blue cassettes. First blue \u000acassette labeled "A. Ca++", contains multiple cylindrical tan/pink tissues (2.0 \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). Second blue cassette labeled "B", contains \u000amultiple cylindrical pink/tan tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Blue cassette A contents (A. CA++), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Blue cassette B contents (B), multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "Right breast pink", consists of two pink cassettes. First \u000apink cassette labeled "A. Ca++", contains multiple cylindrical tan/pink tissues \u000a(1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). Second pink cassette labeled "B", contains \u000amultiple cylindrical yellow/tan tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Pink cassette A contents (A. Ca++), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Pink cassette B contents (B), multi frags, ESS. \u000aLM/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
