ctions demonstrate the atypia to better advantage and a diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on low grade ductal carcinoma in-situ is favored. An excision to fully characterize the process is recommended. Drs Sgroi and Lerwill have reviewed this case and concur with the interpretation. Dr. Michelle Specht was notified of the additional findings on REMOVED_DATE  Addendum #1 by Ronald Balassanian M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : BREAST (LEFT), CORE BIOPSY [report_end] 
