VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-3 Results To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Gregor Krings, M.D., Ph.D. Frozen Section Resident: Valentina Nardi, M.D. Signed Out by: Elena F Brachtel, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Left breast DCIS. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO LYMPH NODES (0/2). (SEE NOTE). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on six tissue levels support the above interpretation. The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed. BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA, SEVERAL FOCI. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND APOCRINE CYSTS. MYXOID FIBROADENOMA (0.8 CM). HEALING BIOPSY SITE. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN and "left axillary sentinel nodes x2", are 2 fragments of tan-yellow soft tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  The larger piece of tissue contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm lymph node, and the smaller piece of tissue contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm lymph node, which is inked blue and bisected. Both lymph nodes are frozen as FX#1, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remainder of the specimen is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN and "left breast", is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.3cm left simple mastectomy specimen, partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm tan-brown skin ellipse, with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm firm, everted nipple, which comes to 1.1cm of the closest inferolateral margin. A black stitch designates the 12 o'clock position. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm exposed hemorrhagic cavity superomedial to the skin, which is exposed to both the anterior and posterior margins. A 3.0cm semicircular healed scar is noted along the skin, which comes to 0.1cm of the superomedial aspect. The anterior margin is inked blue, and the posterior black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal the above mentioned cavity. The parenchyma consists of diffuse dense gray-white fibrous tissue, with focal nodularity. No discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities are identified. Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals no apparent lymph nodes. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Cavity to closest margin, with cavity to nipple as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and cavity to closest posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative upper outer quadrant. Also received in the same container is a 5 x 2 x 1cm portion of tan-red fibrofatty tissue and a REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm strip of tan-pink skin, excised to a depth of 0.4cm  Representative sections of the additional tissue fragments are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION # 1; LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODES  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 25,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:09:32PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART B: Breast (Left), Simple Mastectomy PART C: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide only) [report_end] 
