ction Lab,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN, "left axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm yellow soft tissue fragment, entirely frozen as FX#1, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Callahan, REMOVE_MRN, "left sentinel node #2", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm yellow soft tissue fragment, entirely frozen as FX#2, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Callahan, REMOVE_MRN, "left breast (492 grams)", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm grossly unremarkable nipple. A stitch marks the 6 o'clock position. The anterior is inked blue and the posterior black. Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ill-defined pink firm mass located 2.0cm from the posterior margin and 1.0cm from the anterior margin. The other remaining tissue has fibrocytic changes. No axillary lymph nodes are palpable. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass with closest anterior/posterior margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from mass. Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN and "right breast simple mastectomy with a stitch on 12 o'clock", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm skin ellipse and an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm nipple. Stitch marks the 12 o'clock position. Anterior is inked blue, posterior black. Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrous tissue. Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY #1), SENTINEL: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION #2; LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY #2), SENTINEL: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #1: QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation: The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) Show strong (3+) over overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #2: RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (131) to chromosome 17 signals (110) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Results at or near the cutoff point (ranging from REMOVED_DATE - 2.2) should be interpreted with caution. Addendum #2 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION #2 PART C: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E: CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION (SLIDE ONLY) PART F: CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION (SLIDE ONLY) [report_end] 
