VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-2 Results To: MICHELLE C SPECHT, M.D. Signed Out by: Ronald Balassanian, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: The patient is a 48 year old woman with a history of a radial scar in the left breast diagnosed on a core biopsy who is undergoing a needle localization FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ADENOSIS AND FOCAL LACTATIONAL CHANGE. See note. Note: An immunostain for e-cadherin is positive in ductal cells and supports the diagnosis. Multiple level sections were examined. BREAST (LEFT), RE-EXCISION: 1. FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS. See note. 2. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ADENOSIS AND FOCAL LACTATIONAL CHANGE 2. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. Note: Multiple level sections were examined. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN and "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm portion of tan-red fibrofatty tissue with a localization wire in place. A short black stitch designates the superior margin, and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin. The posterior margin is inked black, the anterior margin is blue, the superior margin is green, the inferior margin is inked yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal unremarkable tan-pink adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the medial end margin en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the lateral end margin en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the tissue containing the silver metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN and "left breast re-excision", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm portion of tan-red fibrofatty tissue with no orientation. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal hemorrhage and focally dense gray-white fibrous tissue. Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm nodular tan-pink granular area consistent with previous biopsy site which abuts the ink. The specimen is entirely submitted from one end to the alternate end as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the end margins en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the entire previous biopsy site as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT),RE- EXCISION [report_end] 
