n 1 focus. \u000a \u000aNote: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated; see individual gross descriptions. \u000a \u000aE. BREAST EXCISION, LEFT LATERAL FINAL MARGIN: \u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, single microscopic focus, present greater than 0.2cm \u000afrom the inked resection margin. \u000a \u000aNote: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated; see individual gross descriptions. \u000a \u000aF. BREAST EXCISION, LEFT MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN: \u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, multifocal with multiple areas of involvement of \u000ainked resection margin. \u000aFoci suspicious for lymphatic invasion are identified. \u000a \u000aNote: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated; see individual gross descriptions. \u000a \u000aG. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA # REMOVED_CASE_ID : \u000aMetastatic carcinoma in 1 of 2 lymph nodes (1/2). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were \u000aexamined on tissue levels from 2 blocks. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: INVASIVE BREAST CARCINOMA \u000aPARTS INCLUDED: A and G \u000aSPECIMEN LATERALITY: Left \u000a \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aTUMOR FOCALITY: Multiple foci \u000aNumber of Tumor Foci: 2 \u000aNote: 2 gross nodules are identified, however invasive carcinoma is \u000apresent throughout the lumpectomy specimen \u000aTUMOR SIZE (LARGEST): REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm \u000aSIZE(S) OF ADDITIONAL TUMOR FOCI: 0.4cm \u000aGRADE: 2 \u000aLYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Present, focal \u000aBLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000a \u000aDISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aINKED MARGIN: Positive, along a broad front \u000aNOTE: This synoptic report does not include results of separately submitted \u000amargins; please refer to appropriate parts of this case for those results. \u000a \u000aLYMPH NODES (SENTINEL) \u000aTOTAL NUMBER EXAMINED: 2 \u000aTOTAL NUMBER WITH CARCINOMA: 1 \u000aNumber with Isolated Tumor Cells: 0 \u000aNumber with Micrometastases: 0 \u000aNumber with Macrometastases: 1 \u000aMETHOD OF DETECTION: Both H&E and cytokeratin immunohistochemistry \u000aEXTRANODAL EXTENSION: Not identified \u000aOTHER FORMS OF AXILLARY INVOLVEMENT: Not identified \u000a \u000aANCILLARY STUDIES \u000aRECEPTOR STUDIES: Requested on block(s)  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By David Curtis Wilbur MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000a \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aA. BREAST EXCISION, LEFT LUMPECTOMY: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed at MGH on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA: \u000a \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR Positive (>90%, strong staining) \u000a \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR Positive (>90%, strong staining) \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN Negative (1+) \u000a \u000a \u000aNOTE: \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  protein are evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria. \u000a \u000aEstrogen and Progesterone Receptor Analysis: Estimation of nuclear \u000aimmunoreactivity of tumor cells. \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or minimal immunoreactivity in < 10% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate incomplete membrane (Focal 2+) or complete \u000amembrane (2+) immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aEquivocal (2-3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000a \u000aExternal and internal controls are evaluated and show appropriate \u000aimmunoreactivity. Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative \u000aresult.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  IHC results are often complemented by  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH analysis, which is \u000areported as a separate addendum. \u000a \u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests \u000aperformed at Massachusetts General Hospital were developed and their performance \u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the \u000aDepartment of Pathology at MGH. They have not been cleared or approved by the \u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000a \u000aReferences: \u000aHammond MEH et al: ASCO/CAP Testing Guideline Recommendations for \u000aImmunohistochemical Testing of Estrogen and Progesterone Receptors in Breast \u000aCancer. DOI: 10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /JCO. REMOVED_CASE_ID .25. REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aWolff AC Et al: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing in Breast Cancer Guideline Update. DOI: \u000a10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /apra. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID -SA. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Elena F Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 17:01*** \u000a \u000aHER-2 FISH Quantitation Analysis \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aA. BREAST EXCISION, LEFT LUMPECTOMY: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aHER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). \u000a \u000aAverage HER-2 copy number/tumor cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aAverage  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  copy number/tumor cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aNote: A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER-2/neu gene \u000aamplification. \u000a \u000aResults are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals to chromosome 17 \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) signals in 30 tumor cell nuclei using PathVysion by HER-2 DNA Probe Kit \u000a(Abbott Molecular Inc.). \u000a \u000aResults near the cutoff point (HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio 2.0) should be interpreted with \u000acaution if the HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio is <2 with the average HER-2 copy number >4 and \u000a<6.0 signals per cell (equivocal amplification). \u000a \u000aReference: Wolff AC et al: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing in Breast Cancer Guideline \u000aUpdate. DOI: 10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID -SA. \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 14:10*** \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000a48 year old female with left breast mass. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT LUMPECTOMY \u000aB: BREAST EXCISION, ADDITIONAL LEFT MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN \u000aC: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN \u000aD: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT SUPERIOR FINAL MARGIN \u000aE: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT LATERAL FINAL MARGIN \u000aF: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN \u000aG: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA # REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aA. Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID  and "left breast needle \u000alocalized lumpectomy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm piece of yellow-white fibrofatty \u000abreast with needle localization wire. The margins are inked black. It contains \u000aan irregularly outlined, tan-pink to tan-white, firm to hard mass measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm  The mass abuts the black inked margin along a broad front. A \u000ametallic clip is not identified. The breast parenchyma shows another well \u000acircumscribed tan-pink firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  located 0.8cm \u000afrom the main mass and abutting the black inked margin focally. The remaining \u000abreast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and pink-white fibrous, which \u000ais dense and nodular focally and shows hemorrhage focally. Representative \u000asections are submitted, including most of the mass and entire smaller nodule \u000afrom end margin to the opposite end margin in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the end margins (shaved and radially sectioned), cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aand  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing section immediately adjacent to the mass, cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000arepresenting sections of the breast parenchyma with most of the mass. Cassette \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  also contains bisected smaller nodule that is 0.8cm from the main mass. \u000a \u000aReceived are 6 containers  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh labeled "additional medial margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm \u000atan-yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the final \u000amargin which is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm firm tan \u000amass which focally abuts the black inked margin. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh labeled "left breast margin inferior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm \u000atan-yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the final \u000amargin which is inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh labeled "left breast margin superior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm \u000atan-yellow portion of