VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000aBoston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  L. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 48) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 18:40 \u000aResults To: \u000aBarbara Lynn Smith MD, PhD \u000aAmy S Colwell MD \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000aA. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA #988: \u000a- No malignancy identified in 1 lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNOTE: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined on tissue levels. \u000a \u000a \u000aB. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA #847: \u000a- No malignancy identified in 1 lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNOTE: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined on tissue levels. \u000a \u000a \u000aC. BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT: \u000a- Focal fibrocystic changes. \u000a- No malignancy identified. \u000a \u000a \u000aD. BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN: \u000a- No malignancy identified. \u000a \u000a \u000aE. BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, LEFT: \u000a- No diagnostic abnormality recognized. \u000a \u000a \u000aF. BREAST EXCISION, LEFT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN: \u000a- Focal flat epithelial atypia. \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD*** \u000a \u000aResident Pathologist: \u000aGeorge Eng MD, PhD \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS \u000aFROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE #988): \u000aNo carcinoma identified; await sentinel workup. \u000a \u000aFROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2; (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE #847): \u000aNo carcinoma identified; await sentinel workup. \u000a \u000aMonica C Chung MD \u000a \u000aOther Pathologist(s): \u000aNicholas A Zane MD, PhD \u000aJonathan H Chen MD, PhD \u000aDennis C Sgroi MD \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  mutation, prophylactic mastectomy. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA #988 \u000aB: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA #847 \u000aC: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT SKIN SPARING \u000aD: ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN, RIGHT BREAST \u000aE: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, LEFT SKIN SPARING \u000aF: ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN, LEFT BREAST \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 6 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "sentinel node, right \u000aaxilla, #988", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue \u000acontaining a lymph node measuring 1.3cm in greatest dimension. The lymph node \u000ais bisected and entirely frozen as FX#1, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Remaining \u000afibroadipose tissue is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "left axillary sentinel \u000anode #847", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm piece of soft tissue, palpated to reveal a \u000alymph node measuring 2.0cm in greatest dimension. The lymph node is bisected \u000aand entirely frozen as FX#2, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining adipose tissue \u000ais submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "right skin-sparing mastectomy, stitch short \u000asuperior, long lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.1cm mastectomy specimen with a \u000along suture designating lateral and a short suture designating superior. The \u000aoverlying REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm ellipse of nipple and surrounding skin appears \u000aunremarkable. The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is \u000ainked black. The specimen consists of yellow, soft, adipose tissue interspersed \u000awith scant delicate fibrous tissue. A small cystic nodule measuring 0.2cm \u000agreatest diameter is present. Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral \u000atissue. Specimen reviewed with Dr. Lerwill. The following representative \u000asections are submitted: \u000a \u000aSECTION CODE: \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire cystic nodule. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin closest to nodule. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral inferior. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral superior. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial inferior. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial superior. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central, with anterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central. \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh, labeled "additional anterior margin, right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm aggregate of multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue. There \u000aare 2 linear vascular clips identified in the tissue fragments. Representative \u000asections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh, labeled "left skin-sparing mastectomy, stitch short \u000asuperior, long lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.3cm mastectomy specimen with a \u000along suture designating lateral and a short suture designating superior. The \u000aoverlying REMOVED_DATE x 2.7cm ellipse of nipple and surrounding skin appears \u000aunremarkable. The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is \u000ainked black. The specimen consists of yellow, soft, adipose tissue with scant \u000adelicate fibrous tissue. Focal punctate yellow foci are noted in the dermis of \u000athe skin. Lymph nodes are not identified in the lateral tissue. Specimen \u000areviewed with Dr. Lerwill. The following representative sections are submitted: \u000a \u000aSECTION CODE: \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin with punctate yellow foci. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral inferior. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral superior. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial inferior. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial superior. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central, with anterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central. \u000a \u000aF. Received fresh, labeled "additional anterior margin, left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm aggregate of multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue. \u000aRepresentative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aImmunohistochemical and in-situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts \u000aGeneral Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics \u000adetermined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of \u000aPathology at Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or \u000aapproved by the U.S.Food and Drug Administration (FDA); the FDA has determined \u000athat such clearance or approval is not necessary. \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA #988 \u000aPART B: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA #847 \u000aPART C: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT SKIN SPARING \u000aPART D: ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN, RIGHT BREAST \u000aPART E: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, LEFT SKIN SPARING \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
