VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-1 Results To: BARBARA LYNN SMITH, M.D. Resident: Thor Stein, M.D. Signed Out by: Adriana Dionigi Corben, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: 55 year old woman status post chemotherapy for locally advanced triple negative left breast cancer. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY: 1. UPPER INNER QUADRANT HEALING BIOPSY SITE WITH NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA (SEE NOTE #1). 2. FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. 3. PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. 4. CALCIFICATIONS IN FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, IN SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND IN BENIGN LOBULES. 5. FIFTEEN LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA (SEE NOTE #2). NOTE #1: The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.1cm upper inner quadrant tumor bed, which includes a healing biopsy site, has been entirely submitted. It consists of vascular fibroelastotic stroma containing lymphocytes, giant cells, hemosiderin laden macrophages and histiocytes. Multiple immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 do not disclose invasive carcinoma [post neoadjuvant chemotherapy Miller-Payne Grading System: grade 5]. There is no evidence of in situ ductal carcinoma. The resection margins are free of tumor. Lymphovascular invasion is not identified. NOTE #2: 8 of the 15 negative axillary lymph nodes show therapeutic effect [post neoadjuvant chemotherapy Sataloff Grading: N-A]. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN and "left breast", is a 23 x 17 x 3.8cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 5 x 4.5cm skin ellipse containing a central 1.4cm in diameter unremarkable nipple. The specimen is oriented with a long stitch designating the lateral aspect and a short stitch designating the superior aspect of the specimen. The anterior resection margin is inked blue and the posterior is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.1cm irregular tan-white indurated area (tumor bed), which includes a biopsy site and is located in the upper inner quadrant of the breast, 1.4cm from the closest posterior and 0.8cm from the closest anterior margin. The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable and no lesions are identified. Within the axillary tail, 15 lymph nodes are identified. Sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 4.5cm indurated area (tumor bed), entirely submitted, with surrounding parenchyma and closest resection margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of the lower inner breast quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of the upper outer breast quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of the lower outer breast quadrant  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node, bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 14 lymph nodes. Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M.D., Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 13,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:17:30PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART : Breast (Left), Modified Radical Mastectomy [report_end] 
